# The shared package is built first because the lint that follows is
# type-aware: ESLint resolves `@cholojai/shared` through its published
# `dist/`, not its source. A stale dist means the linter reads declarations
# from before the change being committed — reporting errors for exports that
# now exist, or missing ones that no longer do. That is the failure that
# cost M5.1 five CI runs.
#
# `tsc --build` is incremental, so this is a no-op costing about a second
# when nothing changed. That is the budget: a pre-commit hook that takes a
# minute is a hook developers disable.
pnpm --filter @cholojai/shared build

# Fast feedback: lint and format only the files being committed.
# Full typecheck and tests run in CI.
pnpm exec lint-staged